Description: Hand the monitor's 3D views to the compositor at their own resolution
 .
 The monitor's stereo layer scaled each view to the area's pixels, so
 the compositor received views Kdenlive had already resized.
 .
 Each view now goes as the frame carries it, never scaled, with the
 area's black bars counted in its own samples: the layer still covers
 the area, and the compositor resizes the whole to it once, so the view
 keeps its shape. The shape comes from the frame's sample aspect ratio,
 which MLT's stereo3d_unpack sets when it keeps a half view half (a half
 top-and-bottom 1920x1080 frame arrives as 3840x540). Views larger than
 a compositor's texture are still scaled to the area.
